bind's configure aborts "Static linking is not supported as it disables
dlopen() and certain security features" when enable_static != no (unless
--enable-developer). The DNS client programs use none of the dlopen'd
machinery the guard protects (named's dyndb/plugins), and a static,
self-contained binary is the point of this package, so make it a no-op.
Patches the generated configure: nixpkgs' bind doesn't run autoreconf.

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index fd20499..a1f1d1e 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -17745,7 +17745,7 @@ DLOPEN_LIBS="$lt_cv_dlopen_libs"
 
 if test "$enable_static" != "no" && test "$enable_developer" != "yes"
 then :
-  as_fn_error $? "Static linking is not supported as it disables dlopen() and certain security features (e.g. RELRO, ASLR)" "$LINENO" 5
+  :  "$LINENO" 5
 fi
 
 
